    description: "[REVIEW 2026-11-01, STALE-FIXED] Reviewed 2026-11-01 on dev 100b6fbb6e. 7ed180a2e7 (WI-surun, 2026-08-28) removed the http_client row. erlang.yaml:141-150 records the removal with match evidence (httpc 10/9 vs http_client 0 on ejabberd/emqx), and status is now provenance_declared rather than complete. Sibling check against local OTP 27: code:which found every one of the 26 row modules in erlang.yaml (application ... supervisor); none are missing. (Original text below; the review entry in the thread has the evidence.)\n\nFound incidentally during the WI-bahid investigation. erlang.yaml:93 declares module 'http_client' with function 'request'. No such module exists in OTP; the inets HTTP client is 'httpc', which is already catalogued at erlang.yaml:90. So the row can never match anything.\n\nWHY IT MATTERS BEYOND ONE DEAD ROW: erlang.yaml declares status: complete, which io_boundary.py:893-898 documents as asserting 'a provenance-backed stdlib enumeration'. A phantom row means that provenance was not checked, at least once, in a catalogue making the stronger of the two status claims. Worth asking how it got there and whether sibling rows share the defect, rather than just deleting the line.\n\nUNVERIFIED BY ME: I have not run an OTP module-existence check across erlang.yaml, only noted this one. The cheap version is to compare declared modules against a real OTP install's module list, which would also settle whether this is isolated."  # 3167
